{"c":[{"id":"97ddef9eec5e365c","sum":"A1/R1 Laya lore: free Laya 422s requests over ~512 tokens, JSON-object state and long choice options, and allows 5 req/min, so Ask cannot run on it; Ask scope is code's reading first (scope-reading.ts); run Laya evals via slow-eval.sh under laya.lock.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"b49778a23660a963","sum":"A1: free Laya 422s requests over ~512 input tokens and allows 5 req/min, so Ask cannot run on it; Ask scope is code's reading first (planner/scope-reading.ts), the heads 'reading' question confirms it, and ask-reading-eval.ts scores readings with no model.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261006T102251Z-3a116bbdf83faf20","text":"A1: free Laya (gateway, boundless) 422s any request over ~512 input tokens (489 ok, ~519 not) and allows 5 req/min per team; heads and corpus fill requests are ~2000 tokens, so the Ask path cannot run on Laya as built (evidence/screen/a1/laya-limits.txt).","type":"note"},{"name":"20261006T102251Z-6d4e95952b64681c","text":"A1: Ask scope is code's reading first (planner/scope-reading.ts; any unread word means no reading); the heads 'reading' question confirms it and intent.agreed skips confirmScope/sectionScope. ask-reading-eval.ts scores readings with no model.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"7bb813feffb3f3c1","sum":"R1: free Laya 422s JSON-object state and choice options over ~300 chars, so Ask-led evals there mostly fail; helper/scripts/slow-eval.sh runs eval sets on Laya in the background (a 429 ends the pass); queue on lockf -k ~/.caret-run/locks/laya.lock.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261006T102855Z-241459cd7cad2754","text":"R1: free Laya gives HTTP 422 for a JSON-object state (harness.ts layaState sends JSON text) and for a choice question whose options total over ~300 chars (heads' scope: 634), so Ask-led evals on Laya are mostly rejected (evidence/screen/r1/probe).","type":"note"},{"name":"20261006T102855Z-7e60ee41200b62c5","text":"R1: helper/scripts/slow-eval.sh runs all eval sets on Laya in the background; a 429 ends the pass and the set reruns from the replay cache. Other Laya users queue on lockf -k ~/.caret-run/locks/laya.lock; rejected requests replay from cache/failures.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"74a3e62ead206367","sum":"Fill joins need one trigger and ordered selectedFormInputs. with-heavy needs free disk minus --est-disk >= 8 GiB (swap counts): ask 3 mem/2 disk for a host build. Merged v2/* may hold a note in two naps; keep one. Chrome joins insertText to the typing undo step: closeTyping.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"8208911c044286ba","sum":"Fill joins need the same trigger and ordered selectedFormInputs. H13: with-heavy refuses unless free disk minus --est-disk stays >= 8 GiB (swap growth counts), so ask the smallest honest estimate (a host build: 3 mem / 2 disk).","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261006T114711Z-5f2b276e7a41de4a","text":"Fill joins require the same trigger and ordered selectedFormInputs: descriptor admission can omit different fields even when input sets match. Different triggers wait with their own captured identity.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261006T132506Z-afeea7cd00f9f436","text":"H13: with-heavy refuses unless free disk minus your --est-disk stays >= 8 GiB, so at about 10 GiB free a 2 GiB build waits; ask for the smallest honest estimate (harness build 3 mem / 2 disk), and swap growth on this Mac eats the same disk.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"2aa517edf32bae42","sum":"I7: merged v2/* can hold one note in naps on both sides; keep one nap. a1-ask-reading once lost names at load ~11. Chrome joins insertText to the open typing undo step (one Cmd-Z took typed text too); setting the caret by script first closes it (insert.ts closeTyping).","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261006T133620Z-cd21a7d05fec9102","text":"I7: merged v2/* branches can hold the same notes in naps on both sides (clean git merge, wake shows them twice); find leaves in two .tree files, keep one nap. a1-ask-reading 'acts on code's reading' lost names once in a default-worker suite at load ~11.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261006T161827Z-f17cd09096e8e827","text":"Chrome joins execCommand('insertText') to the open typing undo step, so one Cmd-Z also removed typed text in a contenteditable. Setting the caret by script where it already is closes the step: extension/src/content/insert.ts closeTyping.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]}
